!!id:"https://tson.io/test-suite/class2/schema/invalid/a-mark-before-the-kernels-record-form-stating-another-extension-expected.tn"
!!import:"https://tson.io/test-suite/schemas/schema-sidecar.tn"
{
  spec: "[TSON-SCHEMA] §5.2, [TSON-SCHEMA] §12.1"
  description: """
    The companion of the plain case, and the one a processor reading the mark as an override gets wrong: the payload
    states `extension: FINAL` and the mark says ABSTRACT. Neither wins, because the grammar has no mark before `!`
    (§12.1): the declaration is a parse error at the mark, not an abstract record and not a contradiction for the
    resolver to arbitrate. The kernel's form writes the one `extension` it means.
    """
  error: {
    category: resolver
  }
}
